City Builder assets and where they come from.

Every asset shipped with the mod is listed here with its source, author, licence and whether it was changed. Assets
whose source or licence is unknown are not added.

Made for this mod (no outside sources), under the mod's licence (MIT, see LICENSE):

textures/block/asphalt.png, sidewalk.png, sidewalk_side.png (the kerb)
textures/block/line/<colour>_<angle>_<offset>.png (the road markings, white and yellow, at 16 angles and 8 offsets:
256 in all)
  Drawn by tools/textures/road_textures.py.

blockstates/*.json, models/block/*.json, models/item/*.json (the paving and marking blocks, and their sunken _low
models)
  Written by tools/textures/road_models.py.

lang/*.json, and everything under data/citybuilder
  Written for this mod.

Data used for statistics only (nothing of it is shipped):

PLATEAU (Japan's Ministry of Land, Infrastructure, Transport and Tourism, and the cities; the cities' site policies,
compatible with CC BY 4.0): building footprints, heights and uses of Kyoto, Kanazawa, Himeji, Tokyo's Taito and Chuo,
measured by tools/assets/plateau_*.py for the lots' sizes, the streets' uses and the blocks' insides.

OpenStreetMap (OpenStreetMap contributors, ODbL 1.0): streets of Kyoto, Kanazawa, Takayama, Hida-Furukawa, Shimoda,
Karuizawa, Nikko, Himeji and Tokyo, measured by the cityMap and osmStats tools for the street network's targets.

textures/block/asphalt.png, asphalt_line_white.png, asphalt_line_yellow.png, asphalt_white.png, sidewalk.png,
asphalt_hatch.png, road_arrow_shaft.png, road_arrow_head.png, manhole.png, drain_grate.png, tactile_line.png,
tactile_dot.png, sidewalk_interlocking.png, sidewalk_granite.png, curb.png
  Drawn for this mod by tools/textures/road_textures.py (no outside sources); the mod's own licence.

textures/block/track.png, turf.png, turf_dark.png, turf_side.png, soil.png, seat_*.png, fresnel_lens.png,
led_panel.png and textures/block/line/{track,turf,turf_dark,soil}_white_*.png
  Drawn for this mod by tools/textures/landmark_textures.py (no outside sources); the mod's own licence.
  Their models and block states are written by tools/textures/landmark_models.py; the seat's steel bracket uses
  the vanilla light grey concrete texture by reference (not copied).
